# /etc/systemd/system/y700-dumpmode-off.service -- started by y700-dumpmode-off.timer 3 min after boot
# Leave Qualcomm "download mode" (qcom_scm.download_mode=full on the built-in cmdline) for the first
# minutes only. With it on, any unclean restart (panic, oops=panic, hung-task panic, watchdog) parks
# the SoC in the XBL crash-dump mode (USB 900E) waiting for a PC to pull a DDR dump - on 2026-10-15
# 03:41 the tablet sat there for 7 h at ~1.6 W (73 % -> 37 %). It also turns panic=10 into "never
# reboots", which defeats the trial kernel's panic -> initramfs count -> rollback design.
# Early boot keeps it: a kernel that panics before /init could otherwise reboot forever and make the
# bootloader switch slots. After 3 min (the trial-kernel confirmation at 90 s is long past) a kernel
# panic means: console-ramoops/dmesg-ramoops to pstore, 10 s, reboot.
# NOT covered until kernel y16: "off" only clears the TCSR dload bits. qcom_scm disables SDI (Secure
# Debug Image) at probe only, and only when download_mode is already off or DT has qcom,sdi-enabled -
# neither is true here (CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE carries download_mode=full). So a reset the firmware does
# itself (watchdog bite, fatal bus error) still goes SDI -> XBL rawdump -> waits in dump mode: on
# 2026-10-31 21:04 a synchronous external abort stopped CPU0 before panic() and the tablet sat there
# 2 h 9 min with this unit active. The 10-15 "verified" test was 5 clean reboots, which write NODUMP
# on their way down anyway. README "10-31 21:04 死机".
# From kernel y16 (patch 1058) writing off also disables SDI and the kernel logs "download mode off,
# SDI disable: <n>" (0 = done; y700-checklist checks it): a watchdog bite then reboots at once (bite
# test 2026-11-01 01:27, ~23 s, no dump mode). Unverified: whether a reset the firmware judges fatal on
# the spot consults SDI, and a bite while the whole kernel hangs (the test bit a live kernel).
# linux/kernel-y16/NOTES.md.
# To take a full dump on purpose: echo full > /sys/module/qcom_scm/parameters/download_mode first.
# On y16 writing full does not turn SDI back on; whether a bite or a kernel panic still dumps after
# that (dload cookie set, SDI off) is untested - try it once with someone present before relying on it.
[Unit]
Description=y700: leave Qualcomm download (crash-dump) mode after boot
ConditionPathExists=/sys/module/qcom_scm/parameters/download_mode

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'echo off > /sys/module/qcom_scm/parameters/download_mode && logger -t y700-dumpmode "download_mode off: a kernel panic now reboots after 10 s (pstore keeps the log); y16+ also disables SDI (see the kernel line SDI disable), so a watchdog bite reboots too"'
